1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,060
You've woken up as Ryomen Sukuna, the King

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:03,660
of Curses.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,020
In real life.

4
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:06,860
You have seven days.

5
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:09,320
At the end of the seventh, nobody in

6
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:09,960
range survives.

7
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,460
In the story, Sukuna was a human sorcerer,

8
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,940
so feared in the Heian era that nobody

9
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:16,740
could stop him.

10
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:19,140
In your version, you didn't eat a finger.

11
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,760
You woke up with all of it, and

12
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:22,160
a clock.

13
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,600
At midnight on day seven, the biggest thing

14
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,300
he can do opens on its own.

15
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,940
It will not ask who is standing nearby.

16
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,180
But first, it's Monday.

17
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,620
You're hungry, and there's a loaf of bread

18
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,140
on the counter.

19
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,540
His technique has two parts.

20
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,820
Dismantle cuts from a distance.

21
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,880
Cleave cuts what it touches.

22
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,980
How hard Dismantle hits depends on how much

23
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:46,860
power you put in.

24
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,620
You point two fingers at the bread and

25
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:49,880
think:

26
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:50,820
cut.

27
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:52,240
Eleven slices.

28
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:53,900
Thin as paper.

29
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:56,980
And a clean line through the bag, the

30
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:58,500
counter and the wall behind it.

31
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,840
Mara, your roommate, walks in with her coffee.

32
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:02,880
"Did you just cut the wall?"

33
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:06,020
"It was already like that." "It was not

34
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:07,180
already like that."

35
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,260
In your version, there's one dial, and it's

36
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:10,880
stuck on loud.

37
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,600
You can't turn it down yet.

38
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,880
Then you see your face in the bathroom

39
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:15,160
mirror.

40
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:17,420
There are dark marks on it that weren't

41
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,100
there last night.

42
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,700
The marks are the first sign that your

43
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:21,560
body is changing.

44
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,260
They'll come back every morning, a little deeper.

45
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,060
And a voice, not loud at all, says:

46
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,080
"Good.

47
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:29,620
Now the neighbour's dog."

48
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:31,720
You say no out loud.

49
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:33,840
Mara asks who you're talking to.

50
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:37,180
In the story, Sukuna is described as sadistic,

51
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,580
selfish and hedonistic.

52
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,900
In your version, that personality doesn't take over.

53
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,200
It suggests.

54
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,560
Seven days of suggestions.

55
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:47,120
Six days left.

56
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,780
Cleave needs contact,

57
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,480
and it adjusts itself to how tough the

58
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,060
target is.

59
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:55,500
It doesn't ask how strong the thing is.

60
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,860
It just opens it.

61
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,160
Mara's bike lock is steel.

62
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:00,420
She's proud of it.

63
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,580
You close your hand around the chain.

64
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,560
It parts like licorice.

65
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,340
"That was a ninety-dollar lock."

66
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:09,020
"It was a bad lock."

67
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:10,700
"It was a good lock.

68
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,280
You're a bad roommate."

69
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,300
In your version, touch is a choice.

70
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:17,760
That's the rule you've been counting on.

71
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,480
At the crosswalk, a stranger grabs your sleeve

72
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,100
to stop you stepping in front of a

73
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:22,320
bus.

74
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,580
A kind man.

75
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:25,940
Your hand moves before you do.

76
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,700
You pull away, fast.

77
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,960
There's a clean line down his jacket from

78
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,140
the elbow to the wrist.

79
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:33,340
He thinks it tore.

80
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:34,900
He thanks you anyway.

81
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,040
Lesson two: kindness is the most dangerous thing

82
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,300
that can happen to you now.

83
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:41,960
Five days left.

84
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:46,140
You cut your own palm with Dismantle by

85
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,840
accident, and watch it close in under three

86
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,280
seconds.

87
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,320
Sukuna can use Reverse Cursed Technique to heal.

88
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,740
Almost nobody in the story can.

89
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,380
Mara stares.

90
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:57,620
"Does it hurt?"

91
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:02,300
"Not anymore." In your version, every heal takes

92
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:03,880
the sleep you would have had.

93
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:04,920
It isn't free.

94
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:05,760
It's borrowed.

95
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,540
By Wednesday night you haven't slept in two

96
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:09,980
days, and you aren't tired.

97
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,620
Our guess is that a human brain can't

98
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:13,820
run this long without rest.

99
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,500
The voice gets louder when you're tired.

100
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,180
That's a guess, not a fact.

101
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,860
"Your friend is afraid," the voice says.

102
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:22,960
"Fear is a form of respect."

103
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,320
You turn the light off and leave it

104
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:25,500
off.

105
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:26,480
You don't need it.

106
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,840
Across the hall, the neighbour's dog barks at

107
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:29,660
your door all night.

108
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:31,580
The voice hums along with it.

109
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,660
At 3 a.m., you find yourself standing in

110
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,800
front of that door, with two fingers raised

111
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,600
and no memory of crossing the floor.

112
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:40,060
You go back to bed.

113
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:41,300
You do not sleep.

114
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,100
You lie there and promise yourself: tomorrow, we

115
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,380
write down every rule.

116
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,720
Mara writes them on the fridge.

117
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,100
Rule one: no touching people.

118
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:53,280
Rule two: no touching animals.

119
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,560
Rule three: if you start smiling, you say

120
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:57,140
so out loud.

121
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:58,540
It's a good list.

122
00:03:59,200 --> 00:03:59,900
It won't be enough.

123
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:01,160
Four days left.

124
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,660
Mara makes you promise:

125
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,320
if you test the next one, she's there.

126
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:10,600
The fire technique, Fuga, only works after Dismantle

127
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,160
and Cleave.

128
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:12,760
You have to say "Open."

129
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:15,120
So you cut a concrete post.

130
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:16,240
Then you touch it.

131
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:17,460
Then you say the word.

132
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:20,660
An arrow of fire crosses the empty lot,

133
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,860
a hundred meters, and takes a dumpster with

134
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:23,100
it.

135
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:25,060
Mara's eyebrows are fine.

136
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:25,940
Mostly.

137
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,880
She says, very quietly: "You laughed." You hadn't

138
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:30,220
noticed.

139
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,980
In your version, that's the line the marks

140
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:33,860
cross on Thursday.

141
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,380
They reach your jaw.

142
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:36,760
The voice says:

143
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:39,680
"Now you understand why I never needed anyone."

144
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,480
In the story, Sukuna fights for the sake

145
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:42,980
of the fight.

146
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,800
Power isn't a tool to him.

147
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:45,680
It's the point.

148
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,440
In your version, that's the temptation.

149
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:49,500
Not the strength.

150
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,940
The relief of not needing anybody.

151
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:53,880
You walk home in silence.

152
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:56,480
Mara walks half a step behind you, the

153
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,020
way people walk near a dog they aren't

154
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:58,560
sure about.

155
00:04:59,260 --> 00:04:59,940
Three days left.

156
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,820
A man shoves Mara at the bus stop,

157
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,520
grabs her phone and laughs.

158
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,620
"Finish him," the voice says.

159
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:09,440
Calm.

160
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:10,480
Almost kind.

161
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,820
Your hand is up before you decide.

162
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:15,200
Two fingers.

163
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:17,680
A clean line already in the air.

164
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,400
You don't throw it.

165
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,580
You throw yourself in front of the street

166
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:22,260
lamp instead.

167
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:23,700
The lamp falls.

168
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:24,940
Everybody runs.

169
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,760
The man drops her phone and keeps running.

170
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,160
Nobody is hurt.

171
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,120
Mara is shaking.

172
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:32,880
"I saw your face.

173
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,800
For a second you looked happy."

174
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:37,460
In your version, that's the real cost.

175
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:38,620
Not the power.

176
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:39,900
What it makes easy.

177
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:42,380
That night she doesn't go to her sister's.

178
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,460
She sits on the kitchen floor and says:

179
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:46,120
"Tell me what happens on Sunday."

180
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,880
You almost don't tell her.

181
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:49,740
The voice says there's no reason to.

182
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,820
Then you look at the list on the

183
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:52,080
fridge.

184
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:53,700
Rule three is still there.

185
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:54,560
You say:

186
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,480
"I'm smiling right now, aren't I?" "Yes," she

187
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:58,700
says.

188
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,860
"Tell me anyway." Two days left.

189
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,360
You tell her the truth.

190
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:07,160
The Malevolent Shrine has no barrier.

191
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,440
It doesn't close a wall around anyone.

192
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,960
It cuts everything in range,

193
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:14,140
Cleave on anything with energy,

194
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,980
Dismantle on everything else.

195
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,080
The wiki says its reach can stretch to

196
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,750
about two hundred meters, using a Binding Vow.

197
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:24,900
In your version, it opens by itself at

198
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:26,080
midnight on Sunday.

199
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,760
You can't stop it.

200
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,280
You can only choose where.

201
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,240
You need three hundred meters of nothing.

202
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,320
You find a quarry, four kilometers out of

203
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:38,560
town, no houses, no road, one gate.

204
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:40,260
Mara reads the map.

205
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:41,920
"You're going alone."

206
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:43,320
"That's the plan."

207
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,660
"That's a terrible plan." You think about calling

208
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:47,080
someone.

209
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,060
The police.

210
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,060
A doctor.

211
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:49,920
A priest.

212
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,500
And saying what?

213
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,220
"A fictional king lives in my body, and

214
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,940
I need an empty field by midnight"?

215
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:59,000
So you spend Saturday doing the only thing

216
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,300
left.

217
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,980
You drive out to the quarry and practice.

218
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,320
You draw a circle in chalk on the

219
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:04,620
gravel.

220
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,740
Then a smaller one inside it.

221
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:09,020
You stand at the center and try to

222
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,220
feel the edge, the way you feel the

223
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,620
edge of a step in the dark.

224
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,040
Our guess is that learning where a power

225
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:17,380
stops is harder than learning how hard it

226
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:17,660
hits.

227
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,240
Nobody teaches that part.

228
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:21,700
By sunset you can hit the edge of

229
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:22,600
the small circle,

230
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,340
twice out of five.

231
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:25,840
Not three.

232
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,200
Not four.

233
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,140
Twice out of five isn't enough.

234
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:30,480
It's what you have.

235
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:31,680
One day left.

236
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,920
11:40 p.m.

237
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:36,400
Your arms are covered in marks.

238
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,080
The voice has stopped suggesting.

239
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,220
It just talks now, like it's always lived

240
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:41,500
there.

241
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:43,680
"Let her stay," it says.

242
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,740
"Loss teaches better than anything."

243
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:47,000
You turn around.

244
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,800
Mara followed you.

245
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:51,740
She's standing a hundred and fifty meters behind,

246
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:53,380
at the gate, with a flashlight.

247
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:54,900
Not far enough.

248
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:58,320
In Shibuya, Sukuna narrowed his Shrine to about

249
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:00,540
one hundred and forty meters to spare Megumi.

250
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,100
In your version, you can do the same.

251
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,140
But a vow isn't free.

252
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,700
You give up the thing you're narrowing for.

253
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,460
You say it out loud: the radius, the

254
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:11,280
number and the price.

255
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,980
You aren't paying with power.

256
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,400
You're paying with the King.

257
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:15,780
All of him.

258
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:18,540
All the marks, all the voice, all the

259
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:18,860
ease.

260
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:19,760
Midnight.

261
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:21,860
It opens without a sound.

262
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:23,080
Not a wall.

263
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:23,920
Not a dome.

264
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:26,120
Just everything in range, cut.

265
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:29,000
The quarry wall, the crane, the old sign,

266
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:29,800
the gravel.

267
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:33,260
Thousands of clean lines, then nothing.

268
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,800
Hundred and forty meters.

269
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,440
Not a hundred and fifty.

270
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,980
Mara is ten meters outside it.

271
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,660
Her flashlight is still on.

272
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,020
The voice says one last thing,

273
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:44,260
very small:

274
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:45,360
"Interesting."

275
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:46,640
Then it's gone.

276
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:48,600
Seven days.

277
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,940
Nobody in range survived, because there was no

278
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:53,560
one in range.

279
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,180
That was the whole plan.

280
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,060
You wake up as yourself.

281
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,840
You're lying on the quarry floor at dawn,

282
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:02,740
and Mara is sitting next to you, holding

283
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,460
her flashlight, which is finally out of battery.

284
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,840
"You smiled for a second, at the end,"

285
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:08,720
she says.

286
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:09,820
"I know."

287
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,620
"You can stop now."

288
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,760
You laugh, and it's your laugh again.

289
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,560
At home, the marks are gone.

290
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,440
The marks are gone.

291
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,920
The bread on the counter is a normal

292
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:24,300
loaf, and Mara has already burned a piece

293
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:24,620
of it.

294
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,180
The wall still has its clean line.

295
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:29,380
The landlord still hasn't noticed.

296
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:32,820
In your version, that's what the title meant.

297
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:35,800
Nobody survives seven days as the King.

298
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,380
Not even the King.

299
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:39,400
Would you have narrowed it?

300
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:40,800
Tell me in the comments.

301
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,920
And if you want the next one, tell

302
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,060
me who you want to become.
